# Development workflow

For any work that changes the repo or produces durable artifacts (code, docs, config, rules, scripts), follow this sequence in order. Do not skip gates. Pure Q&A with no file changes may answer directly.

## 1. Interview (before planning)

Ask clarifying questions until the issue, ask, success criteria, constraints, and out-of-scope items are clear. Do not draft a plan or touch files until enough is known.

## 2. Plan (before implementation)

Present a concise plan for tweaking/approval. Include scope, approach, files/areas touched, and risks. **Stop and wait** for explicit approval. Do not implement, branch, or commit until approved.

## 3. Feature branch (after approval)

Create and check out a Git feature branch before making changes. Capture all work on that branch.

- Naming: `feature/<short-kebab-description>` (or `fix/` / `docs/` when more accurate)
- Do not commit to `main`

## 4. Testing plan (when work is complete)

When implementation is done, present a step-by-step QA/testing plan the user can run. **Stop and wait**. Do not commit, push, merge, or “finish up” until the user says so.

## 5. Finish up (only when user says “Finish up”)

On **Finish up**, run this sequence exactly:

1. Commit all relevant work on the feature branch (follow repo commit rules; no secrets)
2. Archive the approved plan on that branch under `.cursor/plans/executed/` (descriptive filename; include the plan in the commit if not already)
3. Push the feature branch to origin over **SSH** (`git push -u origin HEAD`)
4. Open GitHub PRs as needed (`gh pr create`). **Merge behavior depends on the base repo:**
   - **Our fork / origin** (`blackrook-io/455AEW-PitBoss`, or this clone’s `origin`): create the PR if needed, then **merge it straightaway** (`gh pr merge` — do not wait for review).
   - **Upstream** (`Turtle1stVFW/SRS-ExternalAudio-Remote`, or this clone’s `upstream` when that is the Turtle1stVFW repo): **create and populate the PR only**. Do **not** approve it. Do **not** merge it. Return the PR URL and stop the merge step so a human (preferably a different contributor than the submitter) can review.
5. Check out `main`, pull latest from **origin**
6. Delete the **local** feature branch. Delete the **remote** feature branch on origin **only** when no open upstream PR still depends on it (if an upstream PR was opened in step 4, leave the remote branch until that PR is merged or closed)

Do not push, merge, or delete branches unless the user said **Finish up** (or explicitly asked for that step).

## Hard stops

| Gate | Do not proceed until |
|------|----------------------|
| Interview → Plan | Requirements are clear |
| Plan → Branch/code | User approves the plan |
| Code → Finish | User says **Finish up** (after QA plan) |

```text
✅ Interview → approved plan → feature/* → implement → QA plan → “Finish up” → commit/archive/push/PR/(merge fork only)/pull/delete
❌ Coding on main
❌ Implementing before plan approval
❌ Push/merge before “Finish up”
❌ Auto-approve or auto-merge PRs into Turtle1stVFW/SRS-ExternalAudio-Remote (upstream)
```
